---
description: Require tests for behavior changes, especially UI
alwaysApply: true
---

# Testing coverage

Every behavior change needs automated coverage before the PR is opened.

## Required

- Add or update unit/integration tests that assert the new or fixed behavior (not only that something rendered).
- Prefer co-located tests next to the changed module (e.g. `Foo.test.ts(x)` beside `Foo.tsx`).
- Run the targeted suite and report the command + result in the PR **Test plan**.
- Match neighboring test style (Jest / React Testing Library / Playwright as already used in that area).

## UI-related changes

When the change touches user-visible UI (components, editors, panels, Explore, query preview, copy/feedback affordances):

- Unit/component tests are required for the logic and interaction you changed.
- Visual verification is also required — see `.cursor/rules/visual-verification.mdc`.
- Prefer Playwright e2e when the bug is about layout, remounting, clipboard feedback, or other behavior hard to assert in unit tests alone.

## Logic-only / non-UI

- Unit tests alone are enough. Mark the PR Test plan visual line as **N/A — logic-only** and name the tests that cover it.
- Do not skip tests because the change is "small".

## Do not

- Open a PR with untested behavior changes.
- Disable, skip, or weaken existing tests to make a change pass.
- Claim coverage from tests that do not exercise the changed path.
